# Claim Language for Focus Detection Apparatus

**Claim 1.** An imaging device focus detection apparatus, comprising:

an image sensor comprising a plurality of pixels arranged in a two-dimensional array, wherein at least a subset of said pixels comprises focus detection pixels, each focus detection pixel including a micro-lens disposed over a pair of photoelectric conversion sections configured to receive light beams that have passed through mutually different pupil regions of an imaging optical system, thereby generating a first image signal and a second image signal corresponding to a phase difference between said light beams;

a phase-difference calculation unit configured to calculate a defocus amount of the imaging optical system based on a relative positional shift between the first image signal and the second image signal obtained from said focus detection pixels;

a subject recognition unit configured to analyze image data obtained from the image sensor to detect and classify at least one subject region present within an imaging field, and to determine a subject attribute associated with said subject region;

a method selection unit configured to select, based on the subject attribute determined by the subject recognition unit, one of a plurality of defocus detection methods, the plurality of defocus detection methods including at least a first method utilizing the phase-difference calculation unit and a second method different from the first method; and

a focus control unit configured to drive a focus lens of the imaging optical system based on a defocus amount obtained by the defocus detection method selected by the method selection unit.

---

**Claim 2 (dependent, method aspect).**
A focus detection method for an imaging device, comprising:

receiving, at an image sensor having a plurality of focus detection pixels each provided with a micro-lens disposed over a pair of photoelectric conversion sections, a pair of image signals corresponding to light beams passed through different pupil regions of an imaging optical system;

detecting, from image data captured by the image sensor, at least one subject region and a corresponding subject attribute using a subject recognition process;

selecting, based on the detected subject attribute, a defocus detection method from among a plurality of predetermined defocus detection methods including a phase-difference detection method employing the pair of image signals; and

calculating a defocus amount according to the selected defocus detection method, and driving a focus lens based on the calculated defocus amount.

---

**Claim 3 (system-level, alternative independent claim).**

An imaging device, comprising:

an imaging optical system including a focus lens;

an image sensor including a plurality of imaging pixels and a plurality of focus detection pixels distributed among the imaging pixels, each focus detection pixel comprising a single micro-lens covering a plurality of photoelectric conversion elements arranged to receive light fluxes from different exit pupil regions of the imaging optical system;

a subject detection circuit configured to identify, from an image generated using output signals of the image sensor, a type of subject present in at least a partial region of the image;

a selection circuit configured to select, in accordance with the type of subject identified by the subject detection circuit, a defocus amount detection method from a group of defocus amount detection methods including:
 (i) a phase-difference method that computes the defocus amount from a correlation between a pair of image signals derived from the plurality of photoelectric conversion elements of the focus detection pixels, and
 (ii) at least one further method distinguishable from the phase-difference method; and

a lens driving circuit configured to move the focus lens to an in-focus position based on the defocus amount obtained by the defocus amount detection method selected by the selection circuit.
